# WPNest — Architecture Rules

## Structure

```text
functions.php              → Bootstrap (requires only)
includes/                  → PHP modules
├── theme-scripts.php      → Assets
├── theme-functions.php    → Helpers
├── theme-action.php       → Actions
├── theme-filter.php       → Filters
├── theme-security.php     → Security
├── acf-block-register.php → ACF Blocks
└── acf-json/              → ACF JSON

template-parts/blocks/     → Block templates
sources/                   → CSS & JS source (no SCSS)
├── css/
│   ├── style.css          → Tailwind v4 entry point
│   └── menu.css           → Navigation styles (imported by style.css)
└── js/
assets/                    → Compiled files (never edit)
```

## Rules

- `functions.php` = **requires only**, no business logic.
- One responsibility per file.
- Never edit `assets/`.
- Keep `includes/acf-json/` synced.
- Block template filename must match the block slug.
- **No SCSS** — the project uses Tailwind CSS v4. Write utility classes in PHP templates; add new design tokens or `@utility` definitions to `sources/css/style.css`.

## New ACF Block

1. Register in `acf-block-register.php`.
2. Create `template-parts/blocks/{block-name}/block.json`.
3. Create `template-parts/blocks/{block-name}/render.php` with Tailwind utility classes.
4. Create `includes/acf-json/group_{block}.json`.

**Rule:** Every new block must include **PHP + Tailwind classes + ACF JSON + Registration**. No separate CSS/SCSS file needed unless the block requires complex pseudo-element or JS-driven state styling.
